  "rationale": "Both answers express the sense 'first/given name'. 'Nama depan' is well attested in Indonesian official usage, while Malaysian sources use 'nama pertama' for the same concept. Malaysian 'nama depan' remains understandable and is not a false friend, so the contrast is a valid preferred-term distinction rather than an absolute prohibition.",
